Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:39:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Version cross-device property saves: PUT honours
 If-Match/baseVersion, 409 version_conflict

- properties gains version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1 (PRAGMA-guarded ALTER; existing rows start at 1).
- GET /properties/:id returns { inspection, version } plus an ETag; list summaries carry version.
- PUT /properties/:id reads If-Match (quoted/weak accepted) or body.baseVersion. A base that is not
  the stored version is refused with 409 { code: "version_conflict", version } BEFORE metering, and
  again atomically in the upsert's WHERE clause. Success returns { ok, updatedAt, version } + ETag.
  No base at all stays an unconditional write (old builds, offline replay).
- The property-count 409 now carries code "property_limit" (+ limit) so the app can tell it from a
  conflict. A malformed base is 400 bad_version.

NOT to be deployed before the app's conflict branch is changed: today it marks the record clean on
any 409 and drops the local edits (see the patch preamble).
